WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.870
[Wil] Bladesmiths,
check this out.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.906
[dramatic cymbal crashes]

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:10.110
[imitating metal vocalist]
<i> Forged in Fire!</i>

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.512
I can't carry a tune
in a bucket with a lid on it

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.648
but I can tell you that here in
this first round of competition

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:20.453
you will use this set
of heavy metal band equipment

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.389
and combine that with
another heavy metal.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.124
There's a cloth on top
of your anvils.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.559
Go ahead and lift that up.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.595
[dramatic music playing]

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.331
That is W1 round stock

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:35.334
<i> that you will have to combine
 using a san mai technique</i>

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.804
<i> with the mild steel
 from these instruments</i>

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.739
<i> to forge a signature blade
 in your signature style</i>

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.108
<i> with a through tang.</i>

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.643
Good luck, Bladesmiths.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.611
Your time starts...

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.780
Three, two, one... now!

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.348
[heavy rock music playing]

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.351
Out here on the Forge floor,

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.419
these guys are raging
against the machines

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:57.090
as they try to complete
san mai billets.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.259
[Jerry]<i> First thing I grab
 is some cymbals.</i>

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.962
Brass won't forge well
with hard metals.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.266
Looks like Jerry's going to use
the brass cymbal.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:09.135
[David] No.
Oh my God, he's got the cymbal.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.838
That's the whole thing.
Dave. [imitates cymbal crashing]

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.207
[Ben] Wait a minute. Why is
that cymbal throwing sparks?

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.376
He's cutting something off
the bottom of that.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.945
No, no, he's cutting through
the cymbal.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.113
The cymbal's throwing
those sparks!

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.882
[Ben] Then that cymbal
isn't brass.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.084
[Wil] What is that cymbal
made of then?

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.019
[Ben] It's coated steel,
or something.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.622
[Brent]<i> I'm thinking
 I need to find the biggest,</i>

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.558
<i> thickest pieces of steel
 I can come up with.</i>

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.893
[David] So Brent,
over on his workstation,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.328
has the guitar stand

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.697
which is made out of a lot
of pieces of steel.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.133
I wanna make all three pieces
match as close as I can,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.601
thickness-wise,
so they heat evenly.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:45.672
<i> I'm rotating my mild steel
 in and out of the forge</i>

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.340
<i> and I'm heading to the press,</i>

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.942
<i> and it's just playing
 this game, leapfrog.</i>

00:01:50.008 --> 00:01:51.578
Playing leapfrog with my steel.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:55.214
[Wil] Thomas is being
really meticulous

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:58.918
about cleaning up those
thin bits of mild steel.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.786
[Ben] I like to see
a clean steel

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.889
but I don't like to see people
waiting an hour to clean it.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.892
[Thomas]<i> I'm worried if I don't
 get my steel clean,</i>

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.594
I can get a bunch of big
delamination marks.

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:11.564
<i>At one point, I realized I only
 need to clean up the side</i>

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.534
<i> that's actually going to stick
 to my high carbon steel.</i>

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.537
<i> But it's just taking
 a lot more time than I'd like.</i>

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.705
[Wil] Look at that banana.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.507
Brent's got a hot banana!

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:24.076
As I'm setting my welds,
I see my blade start to

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:26.012
take the infamous banana shape.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.614
What he did was take
a big flat piece of steel

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.716
and put a little piece
of mild top and bottom.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.652
As you flatten that all out,

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.454
the extra steel stretches
more than the other steel

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.757
and so it starts to curve
around and around.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.494
[Brent]<i> So I'm constantly having
 to take the banana out.</i>

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.163
I'm in that chasing-my-tail
game right now.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.398
<i> But I'm able to keep up
 with it.</i>

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:46.799
<i> It didn't get away from me.</i>

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.435
<i> I could manage it.</i>

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.671
So Tom is heading over
to the welding station,

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:53.606
finally.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:57.176
He's trying to get
his welds set up.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.345
[Thomas]
<i> I realize that the piece</i>

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.480
<i> I tack welded onto the steel,</i>

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:04.116
<i> the side that I cleaned up
 is on the outside.</i>

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.520
<i> And I think trying
 to clean it up</i>

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.722
is just going to take
way too much time,

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.624
<i>so I decide to just run with it</i>

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.859
and hope for the best
at this point.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.294
[dramatic music playing]

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.196
[David] Oh...
That didn't look good.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.264
Thomas's blade,
when he was just hammering it,

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:22.234
it looked like a whole section
just blistered.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.970
That wouldn't surprise me
at all,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.671
that thin material.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.573
All you can do when something
blisters like that

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:30.076
is you have to cut a groove
or drill a hole or something

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.878
to allow that gas to escape.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.546
-Okay.
-Then weld it back together.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.281
[Thomas] I just put
a slit in it,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.418
so we'll see if it...
if it takes.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.655
I got this thing
forge welded together

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:46.125
<i> so I go and start
 getting a knife shape.</i>

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.893
[Doug] So with
heavy metal music,

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.495
is there a slow version?

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:52.164
Because Jerry is moving
at a slow tempo.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.167
That heat must have
fatigued him a lot.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.201
[David] Jerry's more into
Pink Floyd, I think.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.137
He didn't quite hit
the heavy metal.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.374
[mellow jam band style rock
music playing]

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.381
[Brent]<i> Lots of things
 can go wrong in the quench.</i>

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:12.285
<i> So I wanna have enough time
 left to correct any errors</i>

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:15.554
<i> or anything that might
 pop up or off in the quench.</i>

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:18.324
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.359
[Doug] Brent just went
for a quench

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.595
with an hour to go.
Good for him.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.030
[scraping]

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.865
Sounds like a pretty good
file test to me.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.534
[Wil] What's going on, Jerry?
How you feeling, man?

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.401
All right.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.003
Are you drinking water
out there?

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.805
-Yes, sir.
-[Wil] All right.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:33.906
Yep.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.974
I think the heat's
gettin' to him.

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:38.278
Let's keep an eye on Jerry.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.347
[Thomas]<i> I forge welded
 the bubble</i>

00:04:42.447 --> 00:04:44.650
<i>and everything is looking good.</i>

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.887
I heat it just to that
right perfect temperature

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.422
and, uh, go in for the quench.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.324
<i> I'm just trying to keep
 a death grip</i>

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:54.927
<i> on that knife
 so I don't drop it in there.</i>

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.296
<i> That's the one thing my wife
 said is,</i>

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:00.098
<i> "Don't drop the knife
 in the quench tank."</i>

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:02.035
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.169
All right.

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:05.705
I didn't drop it.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:07.973
Bladesmiths!

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:08.974
Thirty minutes!

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.777
[tense music playing]

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:14.480
Jerry just quenched.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.114
I mean, he had all of those

00:05:16.214 --> 00:05:18.417
really thin sections of cymbal

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.886
and we didn't think
that was gonna forge weld up,

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.255
and look at him go.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.357
[Doug] Jerry upped the tempo.
Look at those sparks.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.058
[Wil] Man,
he's really going at it.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:27.460
Twenty minutes, bladesmiths.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.929
[Ben] Jerry's taking the slowest
method to do this guard.

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:34.233
I mean, we have Dremel bits
over there that are very fast

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.068
and Jerry's got
a chainsaw file

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:37.603
and slowly connecting the holes.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.739
Honestly, if I was
right where he was,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.041
I'd be sweatin'.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.511
[Jerry]<i> I'm just getting
 this guard filed out.</i>

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.612
<i> And...</i>

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.481
<i> things started going wrong.</i>

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.750
<i> I'm lightheaded.</i>

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.619
<i> They're asking if I'm okay.</i>

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.088
-I'm not.
-[man] Okay.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.357
Something wrong
going on with Jerry right now.

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.692
-[mumbles]
-Get Jerry a chair.

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:02.495
Know where you're at?
Know what's going on?

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:03.596
Get him off his feet,

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:05.131
Come on. Gotta sit down, okay?

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.599
-Jerry is not looking good.
-There we go.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.568
[Wil] I don't think Jerry's
quitting on himself.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.503
I think he's pushed himself
to the point

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.840
of physical
and mental exhaustion

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.542
and it's just taken its toll
right now.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.577
[Jerry]<i> I just realize
 that the smartest thing for me</i>

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.345
<i> is go over and sit
 on the couch</i>

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:22.915
and get oxygen
and take care of myself.

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:24.517
[sighs]

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:29.354
Five, four, three, two, one.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:31.223
Bladesmiths,
shut down your machines.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.291
Drop your tools.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.026
This second round
of competition

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:35.395
is over!

00:06:36.561 --> 00:06:38.164
-Great job.
-Good job, man.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.565
-Where's Jerry at?
-Where he at?

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.300
[Thomas]<i> I look around
 to see Jerry.</i>

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.135
[Brent]<i> We didn't know
 if he'd finished early.</i>

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:46.672
We didn't have any idea he had
to be taken off the floor.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:51.176
[Wil] Bladesmiths, each of you
was to have finished

00:06:51.276 --> 00:06:53.278
a 12- to 14-inch signature blade

00:06:53.311 --> 00:06:55.348
with a steel guard and pommel.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:58.184 line:0%
<i> Brent, looks like
 you've got a solid blade there</i>

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:00.753 line:0%
<i> with a nicely finished
 walnut handle.</i>

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.023 line:0%
<i> Thomas, you've also got
 a complete knife</i>

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.625 line:0%
<i> with a Micarta and steel setup
 on the handle.</i>

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:10.729 line:0%
<i> Jerry... unfortunately, since
 you didn't finish your blade,</i>

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:13.232 line:0%
<i> there will be
 no testing round today.</i>

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.700
What happened out there?

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.436
Well, I was exhausted
from the first round

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:20.339
and just totally dehydrated
and...

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:22.341
and thought, "Man,
I'm sweating.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.409
I need to go over
and get a drink of water."

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:26.478
Next thing you know,
I'm going out.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:29.582
[splutters] You know,
I'm not a young guy, so...

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:32.117
I thought I was up
for the challenge and...

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:33.385
I was close.

00:07:33.485 --> 00:07:34.687
Jerry, you fought hard

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.054
through that first round,

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:37.690
but unfortunately,

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.192
you just
didn't finish your work.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.893
And for that reason,
I have to ask you

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.228
to please shake our hands,

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:44.096
and then please leave
the Forge.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:45.598
Come on forward, my friend.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.365
[dramatic music playing]

00:07:47.432 --> 00:07:48.667
[Jerry]
<i> This is not easy, man.</i>

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:51.203
<i> I thought I was in shape,
 you know, working out,</i>

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:53.172
getting ready for this thing.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.508
<i> It, uh... takes a lot
 of the physical,</i>

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:59.478
<i> mental ability
 to do something like this.</i>

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:03.015
<i> So I may not be
 the</i> Forged in Fire<i> champion,</i>

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.951
but it was a great experience.

